OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F181A1773426106
OL,1,Vk4                               G3/15
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGUSSR ENDS COMMUNIST
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGPOWER MONOPOLY
OL,4,D
OL,5, The Soviet parliament has voted to end
OL,6, the Communist party's monopoly on power
OL,7, and bring in a multi-party system.
OL,9,FThe decision ends the Communist party's
OL,10,F70-year-old hold on the political
OL,11,Fsystem and paves the way for new
OL,12,Fpolitical parties.
OL,14,FThe vote was approved by 1,771 of the
OL,15,Fdeputies with 164 voting against and 74
OL,16,Fabstentions.
OL,18,FThe parliament also passed a law
OL,19,Fallowing the private ownership of
OL,20,Ffactories.
OL,22,D]F This Ceefax page is fromG13-03-90
OL,23,D]F Much more at: teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,182,190,120,250,0,100
PN,18104
SC,0004
CT,8,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F181A1773426106
OL,1,Vk4          j7j5                G4/15
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~s ju?j5j5~sG
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5p j5 j5oz5pG
OL,5, Mr Gorbachev has won the additional
OL,6, powers he was seeking for a new-style
OL,7, Soviet presidency.
OL,9,FIn the parliamentary debate he won the
OL,10,Fright for the president to propose
OL,11,Flegislation and veto laws passed by
OL,12,Fthe Supreme Soviet.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FThe president was given the right to
OL,15,Fdeclare war, martial law and overrule
OL,16,Fcabinet members.
OL,17,F
OL,18,FThe measure was carried, after some
OL,19,Fprevarication yesterday, by a very
OL,20,Fconvincing majority.
OL,21,F
OL,22,D]F This Ceefax page is fromG13-03-90
OL,23,D]F Much more at: teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,182,190,120,250,0,100
PN,18105
SC,0005
CT,8,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F181A1773426106
OL,1,Vk4          j7   h4              G5/15
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~s j7*u?j?h7`s}
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5p juj5j5j5ju
OL,5, Mr Gorbachev offered some concessions
OL,6, to deputies during the debate on new
OL,7, presidential powers.
OL,9,FThe president was given the right to
OL,10,Fveto parliamentary bills, but only
OL,11,Fonce instead of twice.
OL,13,FRestrictions were also imposed on his
OL,14,Fpower to declare a state of emergency.
OL,15,FHe now has to consult the leadership of
OL,16,Fa republic before taking the step and,
OL,17,Fif refused, consult parliament.
OL,19,FThese amendments helped to persuade
OL,20,F1,817 deputies to support the measures
OL,21,Fwith only 133 voting against.
OL,23,T]FFromG13-03-90F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
