OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGIRISH COURT FREES
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGCONVICTED TERRORISTS
OL,4,D
OL,5, The Irish Supreme Court has ordered the
OL,6, release of two convicted IRA men who
OL,7, escaped from the Maze prison in 1983.
OL,9,FIt refused to extradite Dermot Finucane
OL,10,Fand James Pius Clarke, both serving
OL,11,Fsentences for terrorism offences.
OL,13,FThe Irish Republic's Chief Justice
OL,14,FThomas Finlay said they could not be
OL,15,Fhanded to the RUC because they risked
OL,16,Fbeing assaulted by Maze prison staff.
OL,18,FAll five judges were critical of prison
OL,19,Fauthorities for failing to act against
OL,20,Fprison officers accused of violence
OL,21,Fagainst republican prisoners.
OL,23,T]FFromG13-03-90F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,182,190,120,250,0,100
