OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGISRAELI PRIME MINISTER
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGSACKS LABOUR LEADER
OL,4,D
OL,5, Israel's prime minister Mr Shamir has
OL,6, sacked Labour deputy prime minister
OL,7, Shimon Peres from the government.
OL,9,FThe 11 other Labour ministers have
OL,10,Fresigned.
OL,12,FThe move came at a cabinet meeting
OL,13,Fresumed after the failure of attempts
OL,14,Fto mediate between the ruling Likud and
OL,15,FLabour parties over disagreements on
OL,16,Fthe first ever talks with Palestinians.
OL,18,FLabour Knesset members will try to
OL,19,Fdefeat the government in a motion of
OL,20,Fno confidence on Thursday.
OL,22,D]F This Ceefax page is fromG13-03-90
OL,23,D]F Much more at: teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,182,190,120,250,0,100
PN,18113
SC,0013
CT,8,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F181A1773426106
OL,1,Vk4          j7   h4             G13/15
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~s j7*u?j?h7`s}
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5p juj5j5j5ju
OL,5, Israeli premier Yitzhak Shamir's
OL,6, decision to sack Labour leader Shimon
OL,7, Peres does not take effect for 48 hours
OL,9,FNeither does the resignation of the
OL,10,FLabour ministers in response.
OL,11,F
OL,12,FNonetheless, the coalition government
OL,13,Fseems certain to fall after a vote in
OL,14,Fparliament.
OL,15,F
OL,16,FMr Peres precipitated the crisis by
OL,17,Finisisting that the cabinet should
OL,18,Fapprove the peace plan put forward by
OL,19,FUS Secretary of State James Baker for
OL,20,Ftalks with the Palestinians.
OL,22,D]F This Ceefax page is fromG13-03-90
OL,23,D]F Much more at: teletextarchive.com
